WEBVTT

00:48:59.488 --> 00:49:01.288
DB: It doesn't get a lot of retweets.

00:49:01.312 --> 00:49:03.803
CA: There's an extent to which
people are embarrassed

00:49:03.827 --> 00:49:06.379
to have the conversation
in public, I think.

00:49:06.403 --> 00:49:08.303
It's, in a sense, mockable.

00:49:08.327 --> 00:49:10.218
People will be there right now,

00:49:10.242 --> 00:49:15.112
sort of finding that tweet about
which part of this they want to mock.

00:49:15.136 --> 00:49:18.883
It's just, the more,
high-minded is the word,

00:49:18.907 --> 00:49:22.198
but the more sincere,
the more earnest any conservation gets,

00:49:22.222 --> 00:49:24.062
the more people want to take the piss.

00:49:24.086 --> 00:49:27.324
Like, is there any scenario or future
where it actually becomes cool

00:49:27.348 --> 00:49:29.084
to talk about uplifting material?

00:49:29.108 --> 00:49:31.083
DB: I think it is for 90% of the people,